    <statement><p>Estimate <m>f(-0.98,2.02)</m> given that <m>f(-1,2)=-4, f_x(-1,2)=-5</m> and <m>f_y(-1,2)=3</m>.</p>
<p><m>f(-0.98,2.02) \approx</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4.04</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f</m> at the point <m>(-1,2)</m>, which is
<me>f(-1+h,2+k)\approx f(-1,2)+f_x(-1,2)h+f_y(-1,2)k</me>
Substituting the given values and <m>h=0.02, k=0.02</m> we obtain the following approximation
<me>f(-0.98,2.02)\approx -4  - 5 \cdot (0.02) + 3 \cdot (0.02)=-4.04</me>





</solution>
